// What <preset> does to a component, as OpenRocket's ComponentPresetSetter does it. kJava holds
// OpenRocket's answers (the probe SpecialSetterProbe of tier 9b, part R2, run with OpenRocket's
// preset files; see SetterTestSupport.h). A row applies its elements through the entries of the
// setter table to a new component in a document whose application has the six presets of the
// example designs (ExamplePresets.h), and compares the part number and the digest of the
// component's preset ("null, null" without one), its name, the values the preset sets, the
// materials the document holds afterwards and the warnings.
//
// The rows with `.bracket = true` have RocketComponent::setIgnorePresetClearing(true) in force,
// as the handler of a component's parameters has for all the elements of a component; the same
// rows without it show what the elements behind <preset> do to the link otherwise.

